// vbn_ur.cpp: VBN 1.001's `u` and `r` commands as a standalone program.
//
// GENERATED by incdec/tools/mkvbn2.py from incdec/vbn2/ and incdec/inc/;
// edit those and regenerate.  (../../vbn2.cpp began as this file.)
//
// The functions below are the ones incdec/ moved out of vbn.exe one at a time
// and verified there: every function plain `u` and `r` run, as decompiled by
// Hex-Rays and corrected (incdec/README.md).  What they called in vbn.exe --
// its C runtime, and DOS through the shim it was ported with -- is replaced
// here by native code.  Nothing else is involved: no vbn.exe, no pe2elf32, no
// shim library.
//
//   g++ -m32 -O2 -o vbn_ur vbn_ur.cpp
//   ./vbn_ur u archive file|mask...   compress (vbn's MAX mode) into archive.vbn
//   ./vbn_ur r archive                restore into the current directory
//
// Archives are byte-identical to vbn's, so each program restores the other's,
// and `r` also restores archives vbn's `b` and `B` wrote.  vbn2 is i386 code:
// the decompiled bodies keep pointers in 32-bit integers and reach vbn's data
// at its own addresses, which vbn2 maps where vbn.exe had it (0x10000000).

